  "answer": "Found it \u2014 the delete was targeting the wrong key for the item.\n\n**Root cause:** The backend's delete endpoint is `DELETE /api/v1/cart/{code}/product/{sku}` (`BasketEndpoint.removeLine`), and its implementation matches the cart line with `shoppingCartItem.getProduct().getSku().equals(sku)` \u2014 i.e. the path segment must be the product's **SKU string**. But the storefront's `deleteFromCart` put `item.id` (the product's numeric ID) in that slot. When ID \u2260 SKU, the backend finds no matching line and returns an empty 204 \u2014 the item is silently never removed (and the frontend's empty `catch` hides the failure). Every other cart call, including `addToCart`, correctly identifies products by `item.sku`; only delete used `item.id`.\n\n**Fix (one line in `src/redux/actions/cartActions.js:163`):**\n\n```diff\n- let action = constant.ACTION.CART + cartID + '/' + constant.ACTION.PRODUCT + item.id + '?store=' + ...\n+ let action = constant.ACTION.CART + cartID + '/' + constant.ACTION.PRODUCT + item.sku + '?store=' + ...\n```\n\nCart items returned by the backend do carry `sku` (it's on `ReadableMinimalProduct`, populated by the cart mapper), so this is safe for both call sites (the header cart menu and the Cart page).\n\n**Files used:**\n- [cartActions.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/source/work/g1_delete_item/source/codex/5/src/redux/actions/cartActions.js) \u2014 fixed\n- [constant.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/source/work/g1_delete_item/source/codex/5/src/util/constant.js) and [webService.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/source/work/g1_delete_item/source/codex/5/src/util/webService.js) \u2014 URL building / how errors get swallowed\n- [MenuCart.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/source/work/g1_delete_item/source/codex/5/src/components/header/sub-components/MenuCart.js) \u2014 confirmed the item shape passed in\n- Backend (read-only): `BasketEndpoint.java` (endpoint contract), `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` (SKU-based line matching), `ReadableShoppingCartItem.java` / `ReadableMinimalProductMapper.java` (item has both `id` and `sku`)",
